<h1 align="center">🚀 Kotlin Fundamentals Challenge</h1>

<p align="center">   A task management application built with Kotlin, exploring the fundamentals of Object-Oriented Programming and the language's core features. </p>

<br />

## About the Project

Aplicação de gestão de tarefas desenvolvida em Kotlin, como parte do desafio de fundamentos da linguagem.

O projeto permite criar e gerir tarefas através de uma interface interativa no terminal, aplicando conceitos fundamentais de programação orientada a objetos e recursos da linguagem Kotlin.

## Features

- Create new tasks with a title and optional description.
- Generate unique IDs automatically using `companion object`.
- List all tasks.
- Find tasks by ID.
- Update the completion status of a task.
- Delete tasks by ID.
- Filter completed and pending tasks.
- Validate data using `require` and `requireNotNull`.
- Represent operation results using `sealed class`.
- Convert tasks into formatted strings.
- Retrieve the total number of tasks.

## Technologies & Concepts

- **Kotlin:** Programming language used to develop the application.
- **Data Classes:** Representation of entities and data manipulation.
- **Companion Object:** Automatic ID generation.
- **Sealed Classes:** Representation of operation results.
- **Higher-Order Functions:** Usage of `filter`, `map` and `forEach`.
- **Collections:** Data storage and manipulation using `MutableList`.
- **Null Safety:** Handling optional values.
- **Java Time API:** Date and time management using `LocalDateTime`.

## Project Structure

```text
src/
├── Task.kt
├── TaskManager.kt
├── TaskManagerRepository.kt
├── ITaskManagerRepository.kt
└── Main.kt
```

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [JDK](https://www.oracle.com/java/technologies/downloads/) installed.
- [IntelliJ IDEA](https://www.jetbrains.com/idea/) or another Kotlin-compatible IDE.

### Installation

1. Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/herlanderbento/kotlin-fundamentals-challenge.git
```

2. Open the project in IntelliJ IDEA.

3. Run the `Main.kt` file.

4. Use the interactive terminal menu to manage your tasks.

## Application Features

The application provides an interactive menu with the following options:

```text
===== TASK MANAGER =====

1. Add task
2. List all tasks
3. Find task by ID
4. Update task status
5. Delete task
6. List completed tasks
7. List pending tasks
8. Task count
0. Exit
```

## Project Goal

The main goal of this project is to consolidate Kotlin fundamentals, explore the language's core features and develop Object-Oriented Programming skills through a practical application.

